    <semantic:textAnnotation id="_ee6039d7-13b4-4c96-91ba-75648bb70e34">
        <semantic:text>Example 2: Bulk Order for Business Customer
Scenario: A business customer places a bulk order for office supplies.

Process Steps:

Receive Order: Order details (business information, bulk items ordered, payment terms) are received.
Validate Order: The order is checked for completeness and accuracy.If any details are missing, the business customer is contacted for clarification.
Check Inventory: Verify the availability of the ordered items.If any items are out of stock, initiate the restocking process or inform the customer of partial fulfillment.
Allocate Inventory: Reserve the required quantities of items in the inventory system.
Pick Items: Warehouse staff pick the items.
Pack Items: Items are packed, often in multiple packages due to bulk quantities.
Print Shipping Labels: Shipping labels are printed for each package.
Generate Shipping Documentation: Create necessary documents such as packing lists and invoices.
Schedule Shipment: Arrange shipment with a freight carrier for bulk delivery.
Track Shipment: Monitor the shipment status.
Confirm Delivery: Verify that the business customer has received the order.
Collect Feedback: Gather feedback to ensure satisfaction and improve future processes.</semantic:text>
    </semantic:textAnnotation>
